📗
  🔩 The shim: the syscalls the standard library does not reach, bound to the
  C++ functions in native/net.cpp. Sockets mostly, and the few other things
  only the system can say. Descriptors are plain integers.

  Statuses, for reads and writes alike: 0 fine, 1 timed out, 2 the peer
  closed, 3 failed.
📗
🐇 🔩 🍇
  📗 Listens on *host* and *port*. Returns a descriptor, or a negative error number. 📗
  🐇❗️ 👂 host 🔡 port 🔢 backlog 🔢 ➡️ 🔢 📻 🔤gvListen🔤

  📗 The port a listening descriptor is bound to, or -1. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🎯 fd 🔢 ➡️ 🔢 📻 🔤gvPort🔤

  📗 Accepts a client, waiting at most *timeoutMs*. Returns its descriptor, -1 when there was nothing to accept, or -2 on error. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🙋 fd 🔢 timeoutMs 🔢 ➡️ 🔢 📻 🔤gvAccept🔤

  📗 Whether a client is waiting to be accepted. 📗
  🐇❗️ 👀 fd 🔢 ➡️ 👌 📻 🔤gvPending🔤

  📗 Connects to *host* and *port*. Returns a descriptor, or a negative error number. 📗
  🐇❗️ 📞 host 🔡 port 🔢 timeoutMs 🔢 ➡️ 🔢 📻 🔤gvConnect🔤

  📗 Reads up to *max* bytes, waiting at most *timeoutMs*. Empty unless 🌡 is 0. 📗
  🐇❗️ 📥 fd 🔢 max 🔢 timeoutMs 🔢 ➡️ 📇 📻 🔤gvRead🔤

  📗 Status of this thread's last read. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🌡 ➡️ 🔢 📻 🔤gvStatus🔤

  📗 Writes all of *data*, waiting at most *timeoutMs* each time the peer stops accepting. Returns a status. 📗
  🐇❗️ 📤 fd 🔢 data 📇 timeoutMs 🔢 ➡️ 🔢 📻 🔤gvWrite🔤

  📗 Closes, first giving the peer up to *lingerMs* to read what was written. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🚪 fd 🔢 lingerMs 🔢 📻 🔤gvClose🔤

  📗 Numeric address of the peer, or an empty string. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🌐 fd 🔢 ➡️ 🔡 📻 🔤gvPeer🔤

  📗 A clock in milliseconds that never goes backwards. 📗
  🐇❗️ ⏱ ➡️ 🔢 📻 🔤gvNowMs🔤

  📗 How much memory the process holds right now, in kilobytes, or -1 where that cannot be read. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🐘 ➡️ 🔢 📻 🔤gvResidentKb🔤

  📗 The bytes of the file at *path*, when it is a file of at most *max* bytes. Empty unless 📑🔸🌡 is 0. 📗
  🐇❗️ 📑 path 🔡 max 🔢 ➡️ 📇 📻 🔤gvReadFile🔤

  📗 Status of this thread's last file read: 0 read, 1 no such file, 2 cannot be read, 3 larger than was asked for. 📗
  🐇❗️ 📑🔸🌡 ➡️ 🔢 📻 🔤gvFileStatus🔤

  📗 The time of day in milliseconds since the start of 1970, UTC. It goes backwards when the system's clock is set back; ⏱ does not. 📗
  🐇❗️ ⏰ ➡️ 🔢 📻 🔤gvWallMs🔤

  📗 What ⏰ said the first time this was asked, which stands for when the process started. The same ever after. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🐣 ➡️ 🔢 📻 🔤gvProcessStartMs🔤

  📗 The process ID. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🔖 ➡️ 🔢 📻 🔤gvProcessId🔤

  📗 1, then 2, then 3: never the same number twice in one process, whichever thread asks. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🎟 ➡️ 🔢 📻 🔤gvNextCount🔤

  📗 Half 0 or half 1 of the key this process hashes names with: 128 random bits, drawn from the system once. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🧂 half 🔢 ➡️ 🔢 📻 🔤gvHashKey🔤

  📗
    How many bytes the thread that started the process has allocated and not
    freed. For tests that look for leaks: 🐘 stays high once memory has been
    used and freed, and a leak that fits into what was freed does not show there.
  📗
  🐇❗️ 🐘🔸🧠 ➡️ 🔢 📻 🔤gvHeapBytes🔤

  📗 Writes *text* and a line break to standard output as one piece, so lines from different threads stay whole. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🖨 text 🔡 📻 🔤gvLine🔤

  📗 Ends the process at once with *code*, without waiting for anything. 📗
  🐇❗️ 💀 code 🔢 📻 🔤gvExitNow🔤

  📗 Makes SIGTERM and SIGINT set the stop flag instead of killing the process, and ignores SIGPIPE. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🧯 📻 🔤gvTrapSignals🔤

  📗 Whether SIGTERM or SIGINT has arrived. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🛑 ➡️ 👌 📻 🔤gvStopRequested🔤
